# F-460 --prefetch: T=6, N in {2, 3, 4, 8}, cold experts cycling through the store, 30 units per point (the median)
pool: 15 workers + the draining host; the host on logical processor 0, its L3 96 MiB shared with CPUs 0-7,16-23
readers: host = the host thread itself; one = a thread beside the host, on logical processor 16; all = 16 threads beside
         the pool's threads (beside the host, then beside each worker in the OS's order); their L3 domains A/B: A A A A A A A A B B B B B B B B  (B = CPUs 8-15,24-31, 32 MiB)
         both = the thread beside the host and the one beside worker 7, on logical processor 24
traffic: one thread beside a worker on the other CCD (POOL_BENCH_PF_TRAFFIC_CCD=B) (logical processor 24, L3 32 MiB shared with CPUs 8-15,24-31) reads X MiB of a 512 MiB region
         during the gap; the sham passes read a separate 256 MiB region.  The workers park as the standing
         recipe has them (STRATA_POOL_SPIN_US=100).
